<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 103,693 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 103,693 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 103,693 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday, compared to 98,782 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Sunday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			21,352	   10,169</p>
<p>    Import cargo			82,341	   88,613</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, four ships were expected to sail and 10 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>Base oil		  5,150	 Jian She-32	 12/1</p>
<p>Palm oil		 18,000	 Wawasan Courage    2/1</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 40,000	 Trade Resolve	7/1</p>
<p>Furnace oil	    25,000	 Miraj		 13/1</p>
<p>Sugar		     2,500	 Winco Pioneer     12/1</p>
<p>Crude oil		73,000	 Johar		  due</p>
<p>Chemical		  7,500	 Bakri Orbitor	8/1</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
